.policy "eslint-no-template-curly-in-string" revision 5
.description "Don't put template placeholders inside ordinary quoted strings; they are not interpolated, so use a template literal instead."
.language typescript
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.mts", "**/*.cts", "**/*.js", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.mjs", "**/*.cjs"

// ESLint's no-template-curly-in-string: a quoted string whose value holds `${` + something + `}`, which looks
// like a template placeholder but is plain text.
//   "Hello ${name}!"   'Time: ${12 * 60} s'     → reported
//   `Hello ${name}!`   "${}"   "$ {a}"   "{a}"   fine
// The test is on the value (escapes applied), as ESLint's /\$\{[^}]+\}/u is. No options.
.violation no_template_curly_in_string(at: node) code "no-template-curly-in-string"
    "Change these quotes to backticks so the ${...} is interpolated, or escape the $ if the text is meant literally."
    suppress eslint "no-template-curly-in-string"
    suppress oxlint "no-template-curly-in-string"
    suppress biome "lint/suspicious/noTemplateCurlyInString"
no_template_curly_in_string(s) :- kind(s, "string"), value(s, v), match("[\\s\\S]*\\$\\{[^}]+\\}[\\s\\S]*", v).
